            "created_at": "2025-08-09T01:36:01.518771+00:00",
            "notes": "In round three, we get our first big power spike in [Snowball Flight](item_770c6b61-98a8-489f-b44e-c1cc65c0cd7d)! With this power you can start to create extra annoying corridors of mini blizzards, or trap enemies alone in rooms. Still try to not waste your main wall cooldown, but you can use the single ice pillar pretty liberally since it's an extra cooldown and isn't as good at splitting teams apart.\n\nIt also gives Mei an excellent movement ability that allows you to escape situations that you wouldn't otherwise live through. Use it to get to high ground that enemies wouldn't normally expect you to get to (it launches you a little and is taller than the normal wall), use it to escape, or play ring around the rosie to stall/extend a team fight in your favor.  You can also place it right next to your wall that you just used to cut off an enemy to make their escape harder or even impossible.\n\nYou have several item options here, depending on what the enemy is doing. [Sturdy Snowfort](item_afbba267-dff5-4018-a8ab-fa743d128d6b) is quite good, you can get up to 40% extra ability energy at a time, and will always have some amount of extra ability energy available for your mini blizzards. [Icy Veins](item_2c403951-4f9b-4390-ad1e-aabaa09a6da5) is also super good here, literally doubling the damage output of your walls \u2013 this item will often lead to really cheeky final blows that neither I nor my enemies expected. If you don't have a lot of cash, go for more blue items to push out either your damage, cooldown reduction, or survivability. I recommend buying [Vital-E-Tee](item_b92e6f1d-3aac-4eec-b027-00c8e1529016) if you couldn't afford it in round two. Take [Coldspot](item_c7a1b659-1656-49d4-af8b-defe4d8d4be3) if you're getting burned a lot, very useful against Ashe ability builds, or some Junkrat/Reinhardt builds.",
